content='Based on the information provided in the filing, American Express was able to retain card members during 2022. The report indicates that the company experienced significant growth in its card-related metrics, including a 23% increase in billed business and a 22% increase in Card Member loans compared to the previous year. Additionally, the number of proprietary cards-in-force increased to 76.7 million, reflecting a successful strategy in acquiring and retaining high-spending, engaged Card Members.

The filing also highlights that American Express focused on broadening the appeal of its products to attract new customers, particularly among Millennial and Gen Z demographics, and expanding its position with small and mid-sized enterprise customers. This indicates a proactive approach to customer retention and acquisition.

